   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Tense changes",
     "texto": [
      "When telling something from a later moment, we often shift the tense: **Estou cansado** → **Disse que estava cansado** (he said he was tired). If the information still holds, the present can also be kept: **Disse que está cansado** (he said he is tired)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The future becomes the conditional",
     "texto": [
      "**Virei amanhã** (I'll come tomorrow) → **Disse que viria no dia seguinte** (he said he would come the next day), if we report from the following day. Time expressions also depend on when we are speaking: **amanhã** can be kept if it is still tomorrow."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "That",
     "texto": [
      "It's joined with **que**: **disse que** (said that). Persons change as in Spanish: **Estou cansado** → **Ela disse que estava cansada** (she said she was tired)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
